From: Martin Pluskal <martin@pluskal.org>
Subject: give the turn tests room on a loaded build worker

The asyncio.wait_for() calls in these two modules allow one second for an
event the runtime sets almost immediately.  Under the parallel test run that
budget measures scheduling latency rather than a real bound, and two tests
(the background-title quiescence test here and the stale-turn-control test in
backend_contract) fail intermittently with TimeoutError.  Nothing in either
module asserts that a wait times out, so raise the budget; it stays below the
60 s pytest-timeout cap even when several waits stack up in one test.

